ical-bills-after-her-death-by-december-2024-her-memorial-campaign-had-funded-more-than-120-million-in-debt-relief/articleshow/134602028.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2023-new-york-mother-casey-mcintyre-arranged-a-fundraiser-to-erase-strangers-medical-bills-after-her-death-by-december-2024-her-memorial-campaign-had-funded-more-than-120-million-in-debt-relief/articleshow/134602028.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T01:53:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134602256,imgsize-844384.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian family in Plano calls police as Texas journalist Sara Gonzales knocks on door with H-1B abuse allegation: 'I was terrified']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134602238.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-family-in-plano-calls-police-as-texas-journalist-sara-gonzales-knocks-door-with-h-1b-abuse-allegation-i-was-terrified/articleshow/134602238.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-family-in-plano-calls-police-as-texas-journalist-sara-gonzales-knocks-door-with-h-1b-abuse-allegation-i-was-terrified/articleshow/134602238.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T01:51:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134602250,imgsize-53598.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Phoenix man keeps 51-year-old home after ASU drops eminent domain case following public backlash]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134601511.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Arizona State University withdrew its eminent domain lawsuit against the historic Louis Emerson House to preserve the property. The decision followed widespread public opposition and a successful campaign led by John Young and Barry Schwartz. They generated substantial support through a petition that collected over 12,000 signatures. The university had filed the lawsuit seeking to acquire the property for a medical campus.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-phoenix-man-owned-a-historic-house-for-51-years-before-arizona-state-university-tried-to-take-it-for-a-medical-campus-after-public-opposition-the-university-dropped-its-case-and-let-the-home-stay/articleshow/134601511.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-phoenix-man-owned-a-historic-house-for-51-years-before-arizona-state-university-tried-to-take-it-for-a-medical-campus-after-public-opposition-the-university-dropped-its-case-and-let-the-home-stay/articleshow/134601511.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T01:11:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134601974,imgsize-1036666.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[74-year-old Ohio woman sues hospital for amputating her left leg. Surgery was supposed to be on her right leg]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134601836.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/74-year-old-ohio-woman-sues-hospital-for-amputating-her-left-leg-surgery-was-supposed-to-be-on-her-right-leg/articleshow/134601836.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/74-year-old-ohio-woman-sues-hospital-for-amputating-her-left-leg-surgery-was-supposed-to-be-on-her-right-leg/articleshow/134601836.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T01:00:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134601853,imgsize-37768.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Iowa developer buys Valley West Mall for $11M, but JCPenney lease complicates plans]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134598322.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Threshold Capital has acquired the Valley West Mall property for $11 million in West Des Moines, Iowa. This ambitious mixed-use development aims to blend residential, retail, and entertainment spaces. Yet, they must navigate a challenging lease agreement with JCPenney that could impede progress. City officials are contemplating up to $110 million in public funding for this expansive project, with hopes of commencing construction following city approvals and finalized site plans.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-iowa-developer-bought-the-58-acre-valley-west-mall-for-11-million-a-nearly-50-year-old-jcpenney-lease-now-stands-in-the-way-of-redevelopment-as-the-city-considers-up-to-110-million-in-incentives/articleshow/134598322.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-iowa-developer-bought-the-58-acre-valley-west-mall-for-11-million-a-nearly-50-year-old-jcpenney-lease-now-stands-in-the-way-of-redevelopment-as-the-city-considers-up-to-110-million-in-incentives/articleshow/134598322.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-01T00:31:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134598797,imgsize-1419389.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['It was like a horror film': How Flydubai pilot was restrained with headphones]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134600343.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Israeli passenger recounted how he and others restrained a co-pilot trying to take control of a flydubai flight. The incident started when a struggle was heard in the cockpit and quickly escalated. After the pilot was attacked, the plane nosedived, prompting passengers to spring into action. They managed to stabilize the aircraft while using headphones to restrain the co-pilot.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/it-was-like-a-horror-film-israeli-passenger-recounts-restraining-flydubai-pilot-with-headphones-after-cockpit-struggle/articleshow/134600343.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/it-was-like-a-horror-film-israeli-passenger-recounts-restraining-flydubai-pilot-with-headphones-after-cockpit-struggle/articleshow/134600343.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T23:27:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134600459,imgsize-957859.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK PM Burnham says may rejoin EU; France, Spain say 'welcome back']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134599792.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[British Prime Minister Andy Burnham has suggested the UK need to rethink its relationship with the European Union. He remarked that Brexit has not lived up to its commitment of regaining control, particularly over immigration matters. European leaders remain open to Britain's return, as polls reflect some public support; nevertheless, any formal talks would be postponed until after the next election, likely influenced by changing public sentiments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-burnham-says-may-rejoin-eu-if-pros-outweigh-cons-france-spain-say-welcome-back/articleshow/134599792.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/uk-pm-burnham-says-may-rejoin-eu-if-pros-outweigh-cons-france-spain-say-welcome-back/articleshow/134599792.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T22:58:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134599970,imgsize-58646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK sees ‘strong indications’ of Iranian role in RAF Fairford incident]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134599686.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[British Prime Minister Andy Burnham stated there are strong indications of Iranian involvement in a recent incident. Five British men were arrested near RAF Fairford on suspicion of explosives and terrorism offenses. They were later released on bail after no explosives were found in the vehicles involved. The investigation is ongoing and authorities are collaborating with US officials for further clarity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/strong-indications-uk-pm-says-iran-may-have-played-part-in-suspicious-incident-near-raf-fairford/articleshow/134599686.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/strong-indications-uk-pm-says-iran-may-have-played-part-in-suspicious-incident-near-raf-fairford/articleshow/134599686.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T22:49:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134599812,imgsize-63170.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ralph Bellamy’s former 1940s Glendale home finds buyer for $4.795 million after just one week]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134599314.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ralph Bellamy’s former 1940s Glendale home has found a buyer for $4.795 million, just a week after hitting the market. The 1.25-acre property features a nearly 4,000-square-foot Tudor-style residence, equestrian facilities, a pool, hot tub and guest accommodations. Bellamy was known for films including His Girl Friday and The Awful Truth.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/ralph-bellamys-former-1940s-glendale-home-finds-buyer-for-4-795-million-after-just-one-week-featuring-nearly-4000-square-feet-equestrian-facilities-and-1-25-acres-of-private-grounds/articleshow/134599314.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/ralph-bellamys-former-1940s-glendale-home-finds-buyer-for-4-795-million-after-just-one-week-featuring-nearly-4000-square-feet-equestrian-facilities-and-1-25-acres-of-private-grounds/articleshow/134599314.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T22:44:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134599533,imgsize-144934.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Biggest ever university donation: Ken Griffin gives $3 billion to Carnegie Mellon, will become member of board of trustees]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134599240.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/biggest-ever-university-donation-ken-griffin-gives-3-billion-to-carnegie-mellon-will-become-member-of-board-of-trustees/articleshow/134599240.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/biggest-ever-university-donation-ken-griffin-gives-3-billion-to-carnegie-mellon-will-become-member-of-board-of-trustees/articleshow/134599240.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T22:22:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134599266,imgsize-94954.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[South West Water fined £7.8 million over hundreds of sewage spills across Devon and Cornwall]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134598241.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[South West Water has been fined £7.8 million after pleading guilty to 18 charges linked to hundreds of sewage spills across Devon and Cornwall between 2015 and 2021. The incidents included 231 discharges at Harlyn beach and more than 336 illegal spills near Bodmin. The company has 56 days to pay the penalties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/south-west-water-fined-7-8-million-over-hundreds-of-sewage-spills-across-devon-and-cornwall-after-18-charges-including-231-discharges-at-harlyn-beach-and-more-than-336-illegal-spills-near-bodmin/articleshow/134598241.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/south-west-water-fined-7-8-million-over-hundreds-of-sewage-spills-across-devon-and-cornwall-after-18-charges-including-231-discharges-at-harlyn-beach-and-more-than-336-illegal-spills-near-bodmin/articleshow/134598241.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-30T21:29:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134598308,imgsize-137037.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US billionaire sent wife to Pakistan, secretly divorced her under Sharia law, paying only $50. 13 years later, Texas Supreme Court cancels foreign talaq]]></title